{"title":"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 34","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The greatest integer that will divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de5ad20921f3435b32f5a6c1a467d56b60d5e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13511$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee7660f47698c989e3ff8d81379facb81546fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13903$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a1255cd1b58087479d13221832f0e60465fd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14589$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and leave the same remainder is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b73ec3cdb08e2b42316de10f0234e7a20f31b569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 28\\quad \\text{(B) } 49\\quad \\text{(C) } 98\\quad\\\\ \\text{(D) an odd multiple of } 7 \\text{ greater than } 49\\quad\\\\ \\text{(E) an even multiple of } 7 \\text{ greater than } 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that 13903 minus 13511 is equivalent to 392. Additionally, 14589 minus 13903 is equivalent to 686. Since we are searching for the greatest integer that divides these three integers and leaves the same remainder, the answer resides in the greatest common factor of 686 and 392. Therefore, the answer is 98, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7ef72cd47d554d4b473d7e68935e75a19c0e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>\"Credit: Skuppi3\"\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME\" title=\"1970 AHSME\">1970 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1970 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1970\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">Problem 35</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph